        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b947166e-0cdd-5675-9a49-269ad236edd8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Glorious Revolution, Wincanton Skirmish\n- Laws: Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711\n- People: James II of England, James VII of Scotland, William III, Prince of Orange\n- Groups: English Parliamentarians, Scottish patrons, Church of Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- The Glorious Revolution, also called the Revolution of 1688, was the overthrow of King James II of England, who was James VII of Scotland, by English Parliamentarians allied with the Dutch stadtholder William III, Prince of Orange.\n- The Wincanton Skirmish occurred on 20 November 1688 during the Glorious Revolution.\n- The Church Patronage (Scotland) Act 1711 was intended to restore to noble and other patrons in Scotland control over Church of Scotland parish churches after that custom had been lost in the so-called Glorious Revolution.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
